course: dictionary
lesson: 15671
title: Thug and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A thug is a violent, rough person. You can often find out what thug means from the words around it. «The police chased the thugs who attacked the shop owner.» Chased and attacked are clues: the thugs were dangerous people who hurt others.
explain: Thug can also be used more loosely. «Jake called Tom a thug for pushing past him in the line.» Jake is not saying Tom is a criminal. He means Tom behaved in a rough, bullying, aggressive way.
explain: Try the swap test. Put "a rough, violent person" in place of thug in «The hired thug threatened the shopkeeper until he paid». Does the sentence still make sense? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: «Thug» is a noun: a thug, thugs.
fact: «Thug» means a violent, rough person, especially a criminal who hurts people.
fact: Informally, «thug» can describe someone who behaves in a bullying, aggressive way.
fact: «Thuggish» describes behaviour that is like a thug's.
fact: Phrases you may see: «a gang of thugs», «a hired thug», «act like a thug».
exercise: «The thugs ran off with the old man's bag.» What is a thug? | A kind helper who carries bags for people | A shop that sells bags | A policeman who rides a bike | * A violent, rough person who hurts people
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes behaviour like a thug's. | * thuggish | quiet | kindly | gentle
exercise: A fan shouts that a football player is a thug after a rough, late tackle. What does thug mean here? | A player who scores lots of goals | * A player who plays roughly and aggressively | A player who wears a red shirt | A player who runs very slowly
test: «Ben's older brother said the bully acted like a thug in the playground.» What does acted like a thug suggest? | Ran into the school hall | * Behaved in a bullying, aggressive way | Played a fun game with his friends | Felt very sleepy after lunch
test: «A gang of thugs broke into the shed at the park.» What is a gang of thugs? | A group of happy singers | * A group of violent, criminal people | A team of park gardeners | A family on a picnic
exam: Which clue in «The hired thug threatened the shopkeeper until he paid» shows the thug is dangerous? | shopkeeper | * threatened | paid | hired
